## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of THP in Linux, on-demand page splitting, and the impact on performance when only a small region is written.

## Key Concepts
- Transparent Huge Pages (THP) and 4KB subpage mapping
- split_huge_page and khugepaged coordination
- Page Table Entries (PTEs) updates and COW semantics
- TLB shootdowns across CPUs and performance impact

## Code Example
```c
// high-level sketch of handling a THP write fault
int handle_thp_write(struct vm_area_struct *vma, unsigned long addr) {
  if (is_hugepage(addr)) {
    split_huge_page(vma, addr);
    // fault restarts, now maps 4KB pages
  }
  // mark dirty, proceed with normal write
  return 0;
}
```

